{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent negative bias: model underpredicts the level across almost all horizons (typically ~+2 to +5 EUR/t needed), especially during rising regimes.",
    "Trend/lag error: forecasts react too slowly to upward momentum; when the last 1–2 weeks show a clear uptrend, add an additional upward drift that increases with horizon (small at days 1–5, larger at days 10–30).",
    "Amplitude compression: model dampens moves (both rallies and follow-through). In strong rallies, scale forecast deviations from the last observed price upward (i.e., increase slope/volatility) rather than reverting toward the recent mean.",
    "Horizon-specific underestimation: the underprediction grows with lead time; apply a horizon-dependent uplift (e.g., modest uplift for days 1–7, larger uplift for days 8–20, largest for days 21–30).",
    "Regime switch heuristic: if price breaks above the recent 20–30d range/highs, treat it as a new higher regime and shift the entire forecast path upward (level shift) instead of expecting mean reversion."
  ]
}
